{"name":"Suede","hex":"#ba8864","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"suede","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of soft leather, made from calfskin, with a brushed texture to resemble fabric, often used to make boots, clothing and fashion accessories."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of suede."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suede"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suede","blocks":[{"text":"Suede is a type of leather with a fuzzy, napped finish, commonly used for jackets, shoes, fabrics, purses, furniture, and other items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Blue_suede_samba.JPG/330px-Blue_suede_samba.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suede"},{"title":"Suede (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Suede are an English rock band formed in London in 1989 by singer Brett Anderson, guitarist Justine Frischmann, and bassist Mat Osman. Drawing from glam rock and post-punk, Suede were labeled \"The Best New Band in Britain\" by Melody Maker in 1992, attracting significant attention from the British music press. The following year, their debut album, Suede, reached number one on the UK Albums Chart, becoming the fastest-selling debut album in nearly a decade. It won the Mercury Music Prize and helped propel Britpop as a musical era, though the band distanced themselves from the label."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Suede%2C_royal_albert_hall_2010.jpg/330px-Suede%2C_royal_albert_hall_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suede_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/George-Boot_Carson_%28Grenson%29.jpg/500px-George-Boot_Carson_%28Grenson%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo